  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image, singleprofile, resnet50) is very weak at 20.8%. With only two data points, the highest-priority uncertainty is whether the RNA baseline can be improved, since RNA is clearly the dominant modality and most downstream multimodal configs depend on a strong RNA representation. Question tested: config_002 (RNA, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the minimal extension of config_001, isolating the effect of using multiple profiles with average-pooling aggregation while holding the encoder constant. This tells us whether the multiprofile+aggregation axis—required for nearly all multimodal configurations—adds value over a single profile. Why best next step: It is a clean, single-concept comparison to our best result, reduces uncertainty about a design axis that gates the entire multimodal search space, and if it improves on 48.5%, it validates the multiprofile direction before investing budget in more complex multimodal or encoder variants."
}

